# No long hyphens in copy

Do not use em dashes (`—`) or en dashes (`–`) in visitor-facing text, meta descriptions, alt text, buttons, or UI labels. They read as AI-generated.

Use a normal hyphen with spaces, a comma, or a new sentence.

```
Bad:  Design, factory, and install — one team.
Good: Design, factory, and install - one team.
Good: Design, factory, and install. One team.
```

Keep ASCII hyphen-minus (`-`) for compound words (`full-home`, `turnkey`) and for phone numbers.
